# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE TEST RUN'S SETTINGS — committed on purpose, and loaded only by tests
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Vite loads `.env.test` in test mode and in no other, so nothing here can
# reach a build: `npm run build` runs in production mode and reads
# `.env.production`, which blanks the development sign-in, and
# `scripts/check-no-dev-login.mjs` fails the build if a trace of it survives.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. Until 18 September the website suite only passed on a machine
# with a hand-made `.env` — and `.env` is not committed, and must not be, since
# it holds real Firebase keys. On a fresh clone, and on the Linux runner, every
# screen test timed out after five seconds: the app rendered the sign-in page
# because the development sign-in was switched off, and the tests were looking
# for screens behind it. Fifty-odd tests, one missing file, and nothing in the
# failure that said so.
#
# Nothing here is a secret. It is the same flag `api/scripts/with-test-db.sh`
# sets for the API suite, for the same reason.
VITE_ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
